    {
      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "To solve the problem of determining the possible degrees of the remainder when a polynomial is divided by $2x^2 - 7x + 18$, we need to utilize the polynomial division algorithm. The algorithm states that any polynomial divided by a divisor polynomial results in a quotient polynomial and a possible remainder. Specifically, for polynomials \\( P(x) \\), \\( D(x) \\), \\( Q(x) \\), and \\( R(x) \\), the relationship is:\n\n\\[ P(x) = D(x) \\cdot Q(x) + R(x) \\]\n\nwhere\n\n1. \\( P(x) \\) is the dividend,\n2. \\( D(x) \\) is the divisor polynomial,\n3. \\( Q(x) \\) is the quotient polynomial,\n4. \\( R(x) \\) is the remainder polynomial.\n\nThe degree of \\( P(x) \\) must be less than the degree of \\( D(x) \\). Alternatively, if \\( P(x) \\) has a higher degree than \\( D(x) \\), the degree of the remainder \\( R(x) \\) must be less than the degree of \\( D(x) \\). In this case, \\( D(x) = 2x^2 - 7x + 18 \\), so its degree is 2. Therefore, the degree of the remainder must be less than 2.\n\nConsidering the degrees of the polynomial \\( R(x) \\) can be 0 or 1 because these are the powers not exceeded in \\( D(x) \\). Hence, the possible degrees of the remainder are 0 or 1.\n\n### Conclusion\nTherefore, the possible degrees of the remainder are \\boxed{0, 1}.",
